  "mother": {
    "preparation": {
      "model_calls": 1,
      "phase": "preparation",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Research coarse-grained parallelism over target bodies i, using threading support available in the unchanged build and at most four workers. Keep each body's j accumulation sequential. Prefer a persistent team across iterations: compute velocities, synchronize, integrate positions, synchronize before the next force pass. Compare serial, two-worker and four-worker variants; assess a general size-based serial fallback for threading overhead.",
        "B": "Research ARM64 SIMD across independent target bodies, not across the j reduction. Process small target blocks with separate ordered force accumulators, broadcasting each source body's coordinates. Preserve reference arithmetic: sqrd_dist is float, but sqrt and reciprocal are evaluated in double before conversion to float. Match rounding and contraction behavior; avoid approximate reciprocal square roots, horizontal reductions and reassociation. Handle arbitrary n with a correct tail, and do not assume SVE availability.",
        "C": "Research memory layout independently of threading and explicit SIMD. Compare the original interleaved Body layout with compact structure-of-arrays storage, converting once on input and once on output. Keep auxiliary storage O(n). Hoist invariant target coordinates and investigate modest source-loop unrolling while retaining one ordered accumulator per force component. Measure allocation, conversion and small-input overhead rather than assuming reduced position traffic guarantees a gain.",
        "G": "Integrate actual programs produced by A, B and C. Establish each standalone candidate's correctness and measured performance, then evaluate promising pairwise combinations and, if justified within the existing budget, the triple combination. Audit arithmetic equivalence, arbitrary-size tails, phase synchronization and binary serialization. Use the unchanged harness and compare against the baseline and strongest standalone candidate. Never assume additive speedups; retain an uncombined candidate if integration regresses.",
        "analysis": "Only the supplied n-body source is relevant. Baseline mean time is 0.655285 seconds over three samples, with four correctness cases passing; no candidate measurements, input-size distribution or numerical tolerance are supplied. The target has four ARM64 CPU cores and no GPU. Ten quadratic all-pairs force passes are the primary optimization opportunity, but gains remain hypotheses. Every tree must preserve all interactions, ascending-j accumulation, constants, ten iterations and force-before-position dependencies. Preserve the binary contract: read an integer count followed by Body records, and output only Body records. Do not change the compiler, target, tests, oracle or budgets, and do not specialize to test values. Passing four cases is not proof of correctness for every valid input."
      },
